Q: How can I pass properties between children/parents A: <p>\But... You're not passing centroid as prop to be able to bind it at all? If you want to bind <code>centroid</code> you have to define it as a bindable prop in <code>Shelf.svelte</code>, so instead of</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const centroid = [
  values.reduce((s, p) =&gt; s + p[0], 0) / values.length,
  values.reduce((s, p) =&gt; s + p[1], 0) / values.length,
  values.reduce((s, p) =&gt; s + p[2], 0) / values.length,
];
</code></pre>
<p>you should do:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const { centroid = $bindable([]) } = $props()

// and then use an effect to update it with your values, something like this:

$effect(() =&gt; {
  centroid.forEach((value, i) =&gt; {
    value = values.reduce((s, p) =&gt; s + p[i], 0) / values.length
  })
})
</code></pre>
<p>Same for the <code>HoverGroup</code> component, centroid is being desctructured as a prop which as far as I know will never be bindable, so you have to explicitly define it as a bindable prop. Keep in mind that nothing in <code>Shelf.svelte</code> (as provided) is reactive in runes mode in case you need them to update dynamically. Then your usage would be as simple as:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;script lang=&quot;ts&quot;&gt;
  let shelfCentroid = $state&lt;[number, number, number]&gt;([0, 0, 0]);
  let whiteboardCentroid = $state&lt;[number, number, number]&gt;([0, 0, 0]);

  ...

&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;HoverGroup view=&quot;hobbies&quot;&gt;
  &lt;Shelf bind:centroid={shelfCentroid}/&gt;
&lt;/HoverGroup&gt;

&lt;HoverGroup view=&quot;careers&quot;&gt;
  &lt;Whiteboard bind:centroid={whiteboardCentroid}/&gt;
&lt;/HoverGroup&gt;

...
</code></pre>
<p>If you don't need the centroid to be reactive you can remove the <code>$effect</code>  and do the <code>centroid.forEach</code> directly on the script. Hope this helps!</p>

Q: Is there a way to wait for a function to finish before running it again? A: <p>There are many ways of doing it. In the following snippet I followed a slightly different path: each (clickable) button has its own delay-flag in the form of the button's <code>disabled</code>-attribute. While a particular button is disabled it cannot be clicked again.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>async function delay(n){
 await new Promise(res=&gt; setTimeout(res,n));
 return true;
}

document.body.addEventListener("click",async ev=&gt;{
  let btn=ev.target;
  if (btn.tagName!="BUTTON" ||btn.disabled) return;
  console.log(btn.textContent+" was clicked!");
  btn.disabled=true;
  // in a real application delay()
  // will your action (as a Promise)
  await delay(2000); // wait 2 seconds
  btn.disabled=false
})</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;button&gt;click me 1&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button&gt;click me 2&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;button&gt;click me 3&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;button&gt;click me 4&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;button&gt;click me 5&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;button&gt;click me 6&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here is a non-clickable paragraph&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: Install npcap silently without npcap OEM Edition A: <p>The following script will automatically download and install npcap unattended, but not &quot;silently&quot; as the installer will be visible during installation.</p>
<p>With always on top and center the window however, it should be very difficult to stop this installation but it will steal the focus.</p>
<p>Here is the script in action</p>
<p><a href="https://youtu.be/K1lzZHSotN4" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://youtu.be/K1lzZHSotN4</a></p>
<p>Save the following script as &quot;install npcap.bat&quot; and run with admin privileges</p>
<pre><code>@echo off
:setup
call :clear_target_vars &amp; call :npcap_set_ESC_variable
if not defined applist.ubound call :create_applist &quot;npcap&quot; &quot;latest&quot; &quot;hashmissing&quot; &quot;sha256&quot; &quot;npcap-1.85.exe&quot; &quot;https://npcap.com/dist/npcap-1.85.exe&quot;
set &quot;target.pid=&quot;
set &quot;target.app=npcap&quot;
set &quot;VERBOSE=true&quot;
set &quot;DEBUG=true&quot;
set &quot;DEBUG=&quot; &amp; REM set &quot;DEBUG=true&quot;
set &quot;target.installer=&quot;
call :search_applist %target.app% DownloadAppList_index
if exist &quot;latest\npcap-latest.exe&quot; ( set &quot;target.installer=latest\npcap-latest.exe&quot; ) else if exist &quot;%%applist[%DownloadAppList_index%].filename%%&quot; ( call set &quot;target.installer=%%applist[%DownloadAppList_index%].filename%%&quot; ) else if exist &quot;installers\%%applist[%DownloadAppList_index%].filename%%&quot; ( call set &quot;target.installer=installers\%%applist[%DownloadAppList_index%].filename%%&quot; )
if not defined target.installer ( call :download &quot;%%applist[%DownloadAppList_index%].filename%%&quot; &quot;%%applist[%DownloadAppList_index%].url%%&quot; &amp; call set &quot;target.installer=%%applist[%DownloadAppList_index%].filename%%&quot;) 
:main

( if /i &quot;[%DEBUG%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo start /b &quot;&quot; &quot;%target.installer%&quot; ) &amp; start /b &quot;&quot; &quot;%target.installer%&quot; &amp; timeout /t 2 &gt;nul

( if /i &quot;[%DEBUG%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo call :get_install_pid ) &amp; call :get_install_pid

( if /i &quot;[%DEBUG%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo call :find_button &quot;I &amp;Agree&quot; ) &amp; call :find_button &quot;I &amp;Agree&quot;
( if /i &quot;[%DEBUG%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo call :push_button ) &amp; call :push_button

( if /i &quot;[%DEBUG%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo call :center_and_focus_window ) &amp; call :center_and_focus_window

( if /i &quot;[%DEBUG%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo call :find_button_exact &quot;Install&quot; ) &amp; call :find_button_exact &quot;&amp;Install&quot;
( if /i &quot;[%DEBUG%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo call :get_button_coordinates ) &amp; call :get_button_coordinates
( if /i &quot;[%DEBUG%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo call :click_button ) &amp; call :click_button

( if /i &quot;[%DEBUG%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo call :center_and_focus_window ) &amp; call :center_and_focus_window

( if /i &quot;[%DEBUG%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo call :find_button &quot;next&quot; ) &amp; call :find_button &quot;next&quot;
( if /i &quot;[%DEBUG%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo call :waiting_for_install ) &amp; timeout /t 3 &gt;nul &amp; call :waiting_for_install
( if /i &quot;[%DEBUG%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo call :push_button ) &amp; call :push_button

( if /i &quot;[%DEBUG%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo call :find_button_exact &quot;Finish&quot; ) &amp; call :find_button_exact &quot;Finish&quot;
( if /i &quot;[%DEBUG%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo call :get_button_coordinates ) &amp; call :get_button_coordinates
( if /i &quot;[%DEBUG%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo call :click_button ) &amp; call :click_button

:end
GoTo :EOF

:npcap_get_installer_pid (input) target.app (output) target.pid
for /f &quot;usebackq tokens=*&quot; %%A in (`powershell -command &quot;$targetApp = [Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('target.app'); Get-Process | Where-Object { $_.Name -match $targetApp } | ForEach-Object { $_.Id }&quot;`) do set &quot;target.pid=%%A&quot;
if &quot;[%target.pid%]&quot; NEQ &quot;[]&quot; ( exit /b 0 ) else ( exit /b 1 )

:npcap_get_button_hwnd_exact
set &quot;target.search.exact.mode=true&quot; &amp; GoTo :npcap_get_button_hwnd_internal
:npcap_get_button_hwnd (input) target.pid target.text
set &quot;target.search.exact.mode=&quot;
:npcap_get_button_hwnd_internal
for /f &quot;usebackq tokens=*&quot; %%A in (`powershell -command &quot;$global:targetPid = [int][Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('target.pid'); $global:targetText = [Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('target.text'); $global:out = New-Object System.Collections.Generic.List[string]; $code = 'using System; using System.Text; using System.Runtime.InteropServices; public class Win32 { public delegate bool EnumWindowsProc(System.IntPtr hWnd, System.IntPtr lParam); public delegate bool EnumChildProc(System.IntPtr hWnd, System.IntPtr lParam); [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern bool EnumWindows(EnumWindowsProc lpEnumFunc, System.IntPtr lParam); [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern bool EnumChildWindows(System.IntPtr hWndParent, EnumChildProc lpEnumFunc, System.IntPtr lParam); [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern int GetWindowText(System.IntPtr hWnd, StringBuilder lpString, int nMaxCount); [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern int GetDlgCtrlID(System.IntPtr hWnd); [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern uint GetWindowThreadProcessId(System.IntPtr hWnd, out uint lpdwProcessId); }'; Add-Type -TypeDefinition $code; [void][Win32]::EnumWindows([Win32+EnumWindowsProc]{ param($hWnd, $lParam) [void][Win32]::EnumChildWindows($hWnd, [Win32+EnumChildProc]{ param($chWnd, $lp) $sb = New-Object System.Text.StringBuilder 512; [void][Win32]::GetWindowText($chWnd, $sb, 512); $ctrlId = [Win32]::GetDlgCtrlID($chWnd); $procId = 0; [void][Win32]::GetWindowThreadProcessId($chWnd, [ref]$procId); $ctrlText = $sb.ToString().Replace([Environment]::NewLine,' '); if ($procId -eq $global:targetPid) { if ([Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('target.search.exact.mode') -eq 'true') { if ($ctrlText -eq $global:targetText) { $global:out.Add($chWnd) } } else { if ($ctrlText -like ('*' + $global:targetText + '*')) { $global:out.Add($chWnd) } } }; $true }, [intptr]::Zero); $true }, [intptr]::Zero); $global:out&quot;`) do set &quot;target.hwnd=%%A&quot;
if &quot;[%target.hwnd%]&quot; NEQ &quot;[]&quot; ( exit /b 0 ) else ( exit /b 1 )

:npcap_get_window_hwnd (input) target.hwnd (output) target.tophwnd
for /f &quot;usebackq tokens=*&quot; %%A in (`powershell -command &quot;Add-Type -TypeDefinition 'using System; using System.Runtime.InteropServices; public class Win32 { [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern IntPtr GetAncestor(IntPtr hWnd, uint gaFlags); }'; $hwnd = [intptr][int][Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('target.hwnd'); $GA_ROOT = 2; $topHwnd = [Win32]::GetAncestor($hwnd, $GA_ROOT); Write-Output $topHwnd&quot;`) do set &quot;target.tophwnd=%%A&quot;
if &quot;[%target.tophwnd%]&quot; NEQ &quot;[]&quot; ( exit /b 0 ) else ( exit /b 1 )

:npcap_center_window (input) target.tophwnd
powershell -command &quot;Add-Type -TypeDefinition 'using System; using System.Runtime.InteropServices; public class Win32 { [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern bool GetWindowRect(IntPtr hWnd, out RECT lpRect); [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern bool MoveWindow(IntPtr hWnd, int X, int Y, int nWidth, int nHeight, bool bRepaint); [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern int GetSystemMetrics(int nIndex); [StructLayout(LayoutKind.Sequential)] public struct RECT { public int Left, Top, Right, Bottom; } }'; $hwnd = [intptr][int][Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('target.tophwnd'); $rect = New-Object Win32+RECT; if ([Win32]::GetWindowRect($hwnd, [ref]$rect)) { $w = $rect.Right - $rect.Left; $h = $rect.Bottom - $rect.Top; $sw = [Win32]::GetSystemMetrics(0); $sh = [Win32]::GetSystemMetrics(1); $x = [math]::Max(0, ($sw - $w) / 2); $y = [math]::Max(0, ($sh - $h) / 2); [Win32]::MoveWindow($hwnd, $x, $y, $w, $h, $true) }&quot; &gt;nul
if &quot;[%errorlevel%]&quot; NEQ &quot;[]&quot; ( exit /b 0 ) else ( exit /b 1 )

:npcap_alwaysontop_window (input) target.tophwnd
powershell -command &quot;Add-Type -TypeDefinition 'using System; using System.Runtime.InteropServices; public class Win32 { public static readonly IntPtr HWND_TOPMOST = new IntPtr(-1); public static readonly IntPtr HWND_NOTOPMOST = new IntPtr(-2); public const uint SWP_NOMOVE = 0x0002, SWP_NOSIZE = 0x0001, SWP_SHOWWINDOW = 0x0040; [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern bool SetWindowPos(IntPtr hWnd, IntPtr hWndInsertAfter, int X, int Y, int cx, int cy, uint uFlags); }'; $hwnd = [intptr][int][Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('target.tophwnd'); [Win32]::SetWindowPos($hwnd, [Win32]::HWND_TOPMOST, 0, 0, 0, 0, [Win32]::SWP_NOMOVE -bor [Win32]::SWP_NOSIZE -bor [Win32]::SWP_SHOWWINDOW)&quot; &gt;nul
if &quot;[%errorlevel%]&quot; NEQ &quot;[]&quot; ( exit /b 0 ) else ( exit /b 1 )

:npcap_foreground_window (input) target.tophwnd
powershell -command &quot;Add-Type -TypeDefinition 'using System; using System.Runtime.InteropServices; public class Win32 { [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern bool SetForegroundWindow(IntPtr hWnd); }'; $hwnd = [intptr][int][Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('target.tophwnd'); [Win32]::SetForegroundWindow($hwnd)&quot; &gt;nul
if &quot;[%errorlevel%]&quot; NEQ &quot;[]&quot; ( exit /b 0 ) else ( exit /b 1 )

:npcap_push_button (input) target.hwnd
powershell -command &quot;Add-Type -TypeDefinition 'using System; using System.Runtime.InteropServices; public class Win32 { [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern bool PostMessage(IntPtr hWnd, UInt32 Msg, IntPtr wParam, IntPtr lParam); }'; $hwnd = [intptr][int][Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('target.hwnd'); [Win32]::PostMessage($hwnd, 0x00F5, [intptr]0, [intptr]0)&quot; &gt;nul
if &quot;[%errorlevel%]&quot; NEQ &quot;[]&quot; ( exit /b 0 ) else ( exit /b 1 )

:npcap_get_button_coordinates (input) target.hwnd
for /f &quot;usebackq tokens=1,2&quot; %%A in (`powershell -command &quot;Add-Type -TypeDefinition 'using System; using System.Runtime.InteropServices; public struct RECT { public int Left, Top, Right, Bottom; } public class Win32 { [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern bool GetWindowRect(System.IntPtr hWnd, out RECT lpRect); }'; $hwnd = [intptr][int][Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('target.hwnd'); $rect = New-Object RECT; if ([Win32]::GetWindowRect($hwnd, [ref]$rect)) { $left = $rect.Left + 5; $top = $rect.Top + 5; $right = $rect.Right - 5; $bottom = $rect.Bottom - 5; if ($right -le $left -or $bottom -le $top) { exit 3 }; $rand = New-Object System.Random; $x = $rand.Next($left, $right); $y = $rand.Next($top, $bottom); \&quot;$x $y\&quot; } else { exit 1 }&quot;`) do set &quot;target.x=%%A&quot; &amp; set &quot;target.y=%%B&quot;
if &quot;[%target.x%]&quot; NEQ &quot;[]&quot; ( if &quot;[%target.x%]&quot; NEQ &quot;[]&quot; ( exit /b 0) else ( exit /b 1 ) ) else ( exit /b 1 )

:npcap_click_coordinates (input) target.x target.y
powershell -command &quot;Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Windows.Forms; Add-Type -TypeDefinition 'using System; using System.Runtime.InteropServices; public class MouseSim { [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern bool SetCursorPos(int X, int Y); [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern void mouse_event(uint dwFlags, int dx, int dy, uint dwData, UIntPtr dwExtraInfo); public const uint MOUSEEVENTF_LEFTDOWN = 0x02; public const uint MOUSEEVENTF_LEFTUP = 0x04; }'; $x = [int][Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('target.x'); $y = [int][Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('target.y'); [MouseSim]::SetCursorPos($x, $y); Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 50; [MouseSim]::mouse_event([MouseSim]::MOUSEEVENTF_LEFTDOWN, $x, $y, 0, [UIntPtr]::Zero); Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 50; [MouseSim]::mouse_event([MouseSim]::MOUSEEVENTF_LEFTUP, $x, $y, 0, [UIntPtr]::Zero)&quot; &gt;nul
if &quot;[%errorlevel%]&quot; NEQ &quot;[]&quot; ( exit /b 0 ) else ( exit /b 1 )

:npcap_wait_until_button_not_disabled (input) target.hwnd target.waittimeout
powershell -command &quot;$hwnd = [intptr][int][Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('target.hwnd'); $envTimeout = [Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('target.waittimeout'); $timeoutSec = 300; if ($envTimeout -match '^\d+$') { $timeoutSec = [int]$envTimeout }; $code = 'using System; using System.Runtime.InteropServices; public class Win32 { [DllImport(\&quot;user32.dll\&quot;)] public static extern bool IsWindowEnabled(IntPtr hWnd); }'; Add-Type -TypeDefinition $code; $deadline = [datetime]::Now.AddSeconds($timeoutSec); while (-not [Win32]::IsWindowEnabled($hwnd)) { if ([datetime]::Now -ge $deadline) { exit 1 }; Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 500 }; exit 0&quot;
if &quot;[%errorlevel%]&quot; NEQ &quot;[]&quot; ( exit /b 0 ) else ( exit /b 1 )

:center_and_focus_window
call :npcap_get_window_hwnd 
if not errorlevel 1 ( if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; ( echo %ESC%[32mFound handle%ESC%[0m of &quot;%target.text%&quot;'s button's top window &quot;%ESC%[32m%target.tophwnd%%ESC%[0m&quot; ) ) else ( if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; ( echo could not handle of top window ) )
call :npcap_foreground_window
if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; ( &lt;nul set /p=Top window hWnd %ESC%[32m%target.tophWnd%%ESC%[0m made... %ESC%[32mforegrounded%ESC%[0m... )
call :npcap_center_window
if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; ( &lt;nul set /p= %ESC%[32mcentered%ESC%[0m... )
call :npcap_alwaysontop_window
if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; ( echo %ESC%[32malways on top%ESC%[0m )
exit /b 0

:get_install_pid (input) target.app (output) target.pid
set /a loop_count=0 &gt;nul
:get_install_pid_loop
call :npcap_get_installer_pid 
if not errorlevel 1 ( if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; ( echo %ESC%[32mFound%ESC%[0m PID of &quot;%target.app%&quot;, &quot;%ESC%[32m%target.pid%%ESC%[0m&quot; ) &amp; exit /b 0 ) else ( if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; ( echo %ESC%[31mCould not find PID%ESC%[0m of %target.app%... ) &amp; set /a loop_count=+1 &gt;nul &amp; timeout /t 3 &amp; if %loop_count% GEQ 10 ( echo Timeout exceeded,%ESC%[31m exiting%ESC%[0m &amp; exit /b 1 ) else ( GoTo :get_install_pid_loop ) )

:find_button_exact (input) target.text or first argument
set &quot;find_button_exact=true&quot; &amp; GoTo :find_button_internal
:find_button (input) target.text or first argument
set &quot;find_button_exact=&quot;
:find_button_internal
if &quot;[%~1]&quot; NEQ &quot;[]&quot; set &quot;target.text=%~1&quot;
set /a loop_count=0 &gt;nul
:find_button_loop
if &quot;[%find_button_exact%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; ( call :npcap_get_button_hwnd_exact ) else ( call :npcap_get_button_hwnd )
if not errorlevel 1 ( if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; ( echo Found hWnd of &quot;%ESC%[32m%target.text%%ESC%[0m&quot; button, %ESC%[32m%target.hwnd%%ESC%[0m ) &amp; exit /b 0 ) else ( if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; ( echo %ESC%[31mCould not find%ESC%[0m hWnd of button containing &quot;%target.text%&quot; in PID %target.pid%... ) &amp; set /a loop_count=+1 &gt;nul &amp; timeout /t 3 &amp; if %loop_count% GEQ 10 ( echo Timeout exceeded,%ESC%[31m exiting%ESC%[0m &amp; exit /b 1 ) &amp; GoTo :find_button_loop )

:push_button
if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; ( &lt;nul set /p=Pushing button &quot;%ESC%[32m%target.text%%ESC%[0m&quot; with hWnd %ESC%[32m%target.hWnd%%ESC%[0m... )
call :npcap_push_button
if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; ( echo button has been %ESC%[32mpushed%ESC%[0m )
exit /b 0

:get_button_coordinates
if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo Obtaining X,Y coordinates inside &quot;%ESC%[32m%target.text%%ESC%[0m&quot; button 
call :npcap_get_button_coordinates
if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo Found location X and Y inside button &quot;%target.text%&quot;,%target.hwnd%,%ESC%[32m%target.x%,%target.y%%ESC%[0m
exit /b 0 

:click_button
if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; ( &lt;nul set /p=Clicking button &quot;%target.text%&quot; with hWnd %target.hWnd%, coordinates %ESC%[32m%target.x%,%target.y%%ESC%[0m )
call :npcap_click_coordinates
if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; ( echo has been %ESC%[32mclicked%ESC%[0m )
exit /b 0

:waiting_for_install
if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo %ESC%[32mWaiting%ESC%[0m until end of installation
call :npcap_wait_until_button_not_disabled
if /i &quot;[%VERBOSE%]&quot; EQU &quot;[true]&quot; echo Installation %ESC%[32mcompleted%ESC%[0m
exit /b 0

:npcap_set_ESC_variable
for /f %%a in ('echo prompt $E^| cmd') do (set &quot;ESC=%%a&quot;)
exit /b 0

:create_applist
:: Usage: call :create_applist &quot;name&quot; &quot;version&quot; &quot;hash&quot; &quot;hashtype&quot; &quot;filename&quot; &quot;url&quot;
:: Check if index is initialized
if defined applist.ubound ( set /a applist.ubound+=1 ) else ( set &quot;applist.ubound=0&quot; )
:: Store fields in indexed variables
set &quot;applist[%applist.ubound%].name=%~1&quot;
set &quot;applist[%applist.ubound%].version=%~2&quot;
set &quot;applist[%applist.ubound%].hash=%~3&quot;
set &quot;applist[%applist.ubound%].hashtype=%~4&quot;
set &quot;applist[%applist.ubound%].filename=%~5&quot;
set &quot;applist[%applist.ubound%].url=%~6&quot;
set &quot;applist[%applist.ubound%].urlreferer=%~7&quot;
set &quot;applist[%applist.ubound%].postdownload=%~8&quot;
set &quot;applist[%applist.ubound%].dependencies=%~9&quot;
goto :EOF

:GetExtension
